  "comments": "<p>1992 saw the changeover from bronze to copper-plated steel for both the 1p &amp; 2p to reduce the cost of production. Both bronze and copper-plated steel 1992 coins can be found, however those in Proof &amp; Brilliant Uncirculated sets were struck in bronze, while circulation strikes were copper-plated steel.<br><br><i>Reverse die varieties:</i><br><br><strong>Type A</strong> <i>(1992-94)</i> Junctions of portcullis bars are raised dots;<br><strong>Type B</strong> <i>(1992-97)</i> Junctions of portcullis bars are incuse circles;<br><br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5df116a6c1ea9.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5df116a6c1ea9.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>Information has been received to suggest that 1993-97 BU and Proof sets were struck with Type B but this is yet to be confirmed.</p>",
